  "turns": [
    {
      "id": "t1",
      "instruction": "Required solver: OpenSees.\nBuild and analyze the attached two-story steel frame in OpenSees. The lower story has two 6 m bays at elevation z=3.6 m. The upper story is 3.3 m high (z=6.9 m) and contains only the left 6 m bay. All three bases are fixed. Each of the three actual beams carries 10 kN/m vertically downward in case D. Report ux, uz and ry at all five floor joints; N, V3 and M2 at every member end incident at setback-edge joints n1-1, n1-2 and n2-1; and Fx, Fz and My at all three bases. Use the attached explicit material, section and axis definitions for first-order linear elastic static analysis with self-weight disabled.\n\nUse all public appendices. Report the complete requested numerical table and the required summaries.",
      "state": 1,
      "expectation": "analyze",
      "attachments": [
        "input-data.json",
        "output-requests.json",
        "analysis-conventions.txt",
